It would be nice to have some sort of per query/mutation options, just like Fastify's [route configs](https://www.fastify.io/docs/latest/Reference/Routes/#config)

Could work like this: 

```js
router<Context>({ hasAuth: true } /* default options, also used for type inference */)
  .middleware(async ({ options }) => {
    /* only check if route has auth */
    if(options.hasAuth === true) {
      // check auth
    }
  })
  .mutation('login', {
    input: ...,
    /* optional options object */
    options: { 
      hasAuth: false
    },
    resolve: ...
  })
```
Possible use cases: 
- disable authentication on a per route basis
- rate limiting settings per route
- ...

